Recipe: Crispy Chicken Fillet
&#xD;
Ingredients:
&#xD;
&#xD;
1 kilogram chicken breast&#xD;
200 grams flour&#xD;
1 medium egg (beaten)&#xD;
pepper&#xD;
1/2 teaspoon garlic powder&#xD;
1 teaspoon paprika powder&#xD;
1 teaspoon seasoning (chicken)&#xD;
1 teaspoon dried parsley&#xD;
200 milliliters sunflower oil&#xD;
&#xD;
Directions:
&#xD;
&#xD;
Preheat oven to 200C.&#xD;
Pat the chicken breast dry with a kitchen paper & set them on a flat service. Beat the chicken breast until it is even in thickness.&#xD;
In a bowl, mix the flour, pepper, chicken seasoning, garlic powder, paprika powder & dried parsley.&#xD;
Dip the chicken breasts into the beaten egg & then cover well with the flour mixture.&#xD;
Heat up the oil in a frying pan.&#xD;
Start cooking the chicken breasts. Fry the chicken for 4-5 minutes on each side over medium to high heat.&#xD;
When finished frying the chicken breasts, put them on some kitchen paper to soak up the extra oil & then transfer them to a baking dish on a baking paper.&#xD;
Cook the chicken breasts in the oven for 15 minutes.&#xD;
You can serve them as is or in burger buns topped with some salad.&#xD;

