Recipe: Beef, Spinach and Rice stew
&#xD;
Ingredients:
&#xD;
&#xD;
1 lb beef (450g)&#xD;
7oz spinach (200 g)&#xD;
3 tbsp rice&#xD;
2 medium sized onions&#xD;
2 cloves garlic &#xD;
1 pc. peppers (red)&#xD;
1/2 pcs. carrots&#xD;
2cm parsnip&#xD;
1 cm ginger&#xD;
1 tbsp. red pepper&#xD;
1 tsp. black pepper&#xD;
1 tsp. oregano&#xD;
&#xD;
Instructions:
&#xD;
&#xD;
The meat is dices into medium-sized pieces.&#xD;
Fry in a pressure cooker with a little fat. Add water, so that half of the pot is full and cook the meat for 50 minutes.&#xD;
Then fry the onion, garlic, pepper, carrot, parsnip and chopped ginger in a pan.&#xD;
When the vegetables soften, add the rice and fry for a little while. Add the red and black pepper and oregano.&#xD;
Pour the vegetables into a saucepan, add the meat and part of the broth - to the desired density of the stew. It needs to be salted.&#xD;
Then add the chopped spinach. The stew is boiled for another 20-30 minutes. Before turning off the stove, the stew is thickened with 1 tbsp. Flour, diluted in a little water.&#xD;

