Recommended Dish: Pan Fried Breakfast Steaks with Mushrooms
&#xD;
Ingredients:
&#xD;
&#xD;
1/2 kilo beef breakfast steak partially frozen&#xD;
1 teaspoon salt&#xD;
1 teaspoon liquid seasoning&#xD;
1 teaspoon ground pepper&#xD;
1 teaspoon calamansi lime juice&#xD;
1/2 cup butter&#xD;
1/2 kilo fresh whole oyster mushrooms&#xD;
1 piece beef bouillon cube&#xD;
1/4 cup all-purpose flour&#xD;
2 cups fresh milk or full cream milk&#xD;
1/4 cup parsley or scallion green spring onions, chopped (for garnishing)&#xD;
&#xD;
Instructions:
&#xD;
&#xD;
Season beef breakfast steak with salt, liquid seasoning, ground pepper and calamansi juice.&#xD;
In a heavy pan, heat butter and fry the steaks on both sides until brown. Transfer steaks to a platter and set aside.&#xD;
In the same pan, add fresh whole oyster mushroom. Saute for a while then stir in beef bouillon cubes and dissolve in butter.&#xD;
Thicken with flour. Cook for about 1 minute then pour in milk. Let boil. Then pour the sauce over steaks.&#xD;
If you want to have a sizzling steak, heat the sizzling plates on a stove until hot. Put the steak then pour the sauce over to have a sizzling effect. Garnish with parsley or scallion.&#xD;

