&#xD;
Before Use:
&#xD;
&#xD;
Make sure the fabric is colorfast and washable. If unsure, test with a cotton swab on a small, inconspicuous area. If any color shows on the swab, do not treat or launder. Instead, take it to a cleaning professional.&#xD;
Not recommended for use on silk, wool, suede, or non-washable leather.&#xD;
Rust, dyes, indelible inks, and bleach spots will not be removed by Simple Green Laundry Stain Remover.&#xD;
&#xD;
Directions for Use: 
&#xD;
&#xD;
Spray directly onto the stain, soaking the fabric.&#xD;
Allow to penetrate fabric for a minute or two (up to 5 minutes for severe stains). Do not allow Simple Green Laundry Stain Remover to dry on the fabric before washing.&#xD;
Fold the stained fabric over on itself and rub the fabric together gently.&#xD;
Launder as usual with whatever other laundry products you choose. Simple Green Laundry Stain Remover will not interfere with laundry detergents or additives (such as oxygen boosters or chlorine).&#xD;
For best results: Treat stains as soon as possible after they occur. Allow Simple Green Laundry Stain Remover to remain wet on set-in or greasy stains for several hours before washing, re-wetting every so often if necessary&#xD;
&#xD;
Precautions: Avoid eye contact.
&#xD;
First Aid Treatment: If swallowed, do not induce vomiting. Drink several glasses of clean water. Contact Poison Control Center or a physician if prolonged digestive upset occurs. If in eyes, rinse with water for 15 minutes, lifting upper and lower eyelids to flush thoroughly.
&#xD;
Contains: Surfactants and preservatives.

