&#xD;
Cooking Directions
&#xD;
&#xD;
Pan-Fried: Preheat and oil your pan. Place the frozen dumplings on the pan and cook for 5 to 6 minutes over medium heat.&#xD;
Oven: Set your oven to Combination Mode (Top &amp; Bottom Level) at 180&#xB0;C, with the steam level at about 20%. Apply some oil to the dumplings and place the dumplings on the oven pan. Cook for 4 to 5 minutes and serve.&#xD;
Steamed: Place dumplings not too close to each other, steam for about 7 to 8 minutes, and serve.&#xA0;&#xD;
Microwave: Place dumplings inside the microwave, covered with a wet cloth. Microwave for 4 to 5 minutes. Ready to serve.&#xD;
Fried: Prepare a deep frying pan. Pour oil until it almost covers the entire size of the dumplings, and preheat the pan to 170&#xB0;C. Place dumplings on the pan and fry for 2 to 3 minutes until they turn crispy and light brown.&#xA0;&#xD;
